Keep movie source PCM separate from ALSA driver silence at end of stream.

Wine 10 WOD_PushData limits client writes to queued wave-header frames.
Its ALSA transport adds a single period-sized lead-in only without pending
client data. The native path instead filled every remaining hardware slot
with zeros as soon as source submission ended, while source samples were
still queued. Wait for consumed source completion before driver silence,
and bound each silence submission by the actual negotiated ALSA period.

This corrects the source/driver boundary; whole original tails and clocks
still require their own comparison. No source samples or times are fitted.

--- a/dd2_native_movie_alsa.h
+++ b/dd2_native_movie_alsa.h
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
